            <ArticleTitle>An efficient single prime protocol for the induction of antigen-induced airways inflammation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jim.2013.06.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-1759(13)00179-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are a number of mouse models of allergic airway inflammation used to delineate various aspects of asthma. One of the hurdles with using mice is their natural resistance to developing a Th2 allergic response. This is often overcome by double priming with the allergen and an adjuvant. Here we report on an efficient 11day, single antigen/alum priming protocol that is sufficient to sensitise mice for the development of Th2-mediated inflammation in the lung following antigen challenge.</AbstractText>
